Certainly! Below is the translation of your text into UVL (Unified Verification Language) code:

```uvl
features
    SecurityTeam
        mandatory
            SecurityArchitect
                alternative
                    SecurityArchitectPerson {Role 'Security Architect'}
            SecurityEngineer
                alternative
                    SecurityEngineerPerson {Role 'Security Engineer'}
        optional
            Manager
                alternative
                    ManagerPerson {Role 'Manager'}
            ScrumMaster
                alternative
                    ScrumMasterPerson {Role 'Scrum Master'}
constraints
    SecurityArchitectPerson & SecurityEngineerPerson == false
    ManagerPerson | ScrumMasterPerson
```

This UVL code ensures that:
1. A Security Architect and a Security Engineer must be present in the Security Team.
2. These roles cannot be filled by the same person.
3. There can be an optional Manager or Scrum Master, but not both at the same time.